					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tl333s" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1304786); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=1304786&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1606984876" alt="TL333s" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=1304786)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/tl333s" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(1304786); return false;" >TL333s</a></span> <span class="odate time_1500490952 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">19 Jul 2017 19:02</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-3398752">
									

<p>This puts me in a fun ethical conundrum, because I sick to death of politicians (anyone, really) who don't care about people, but at the same time, I am overwhelmingly opposed to mind control. Despite what the SERD might say on that note.</p>
<div class="collapsible-block">
<div class="collapsible-block-folded"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">+&nbsp;Tangentially&nbsp;related&nbsp;rambling</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded" style="display:none">
<div class="collapsible-block-unfolded-link"><a class="collapsible-block-link" href="javascript:;">–&nbsp;hide&nbsp;block</a></div>
<div class="collapsible-block-content">
<p>Y'know, it strikes me that this article is indicative of a direction in which the wiki is headed. And I swear, this isn't me telling you kids to get your cognitohazards off my lawn.</p>
<p>Back when I joined up, GoIs were always these nebulous things. Like, you could gather the modus operandi for Wondertainment or the Factory, but what they were, what they <em>represented</em>? Not so much. It was always this shadowy suggestion of, &quot;Oh, this comes from Marshall, Carter &amp; Dark! We've maybe heard of them once before. They're always out there, lurking and watching!&quot;</p>
<p>Compare that to the passage in the addendum where the researcher is all, &quot;Yeah, MCF definitely could not have made this themselves. I'm thinking MC&amp;D, but it's probably above them, too.&quot; Like, that never would have happened back in Series II, let alone Series I. It would just be so out of place. But now we're kind of getting into building a world that's more interconnected, where the Foundation is occasionally willing to work alongside GoIs &#8212; and this is hardly the first or deepest article to suggest that they would &#8212; and I kinda like that. I mean, it's different than what I'm used to, I'll probably never be able to utilize it properly in an article myself, but if the wiki's gonna change, I think this is a change I can support.</p>
<p>So, uh, good job with that. :B Or something. Ya darn kids.</p>
</div>
